HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppcciiccoonnff utility appeared first in FreeBSD 2.2.  The --aa option was
     added for PCI KLD support in FreeBSD 3.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The ppcciiccoonnff utility was written by Stefan Esser and Garrett Wollman.

BBUUGGSS
     The --bb and --hh options are implemented in ppcciiccoonnff, but not in the underly‐
     ing ioctl(2).

     It might be useful to give non-root users access to the --aa and --rr op‐
     tions.  But only root will be able to execute a kkllddllooaadd to provide the
     device with a driver KLD, and reading of configuration space registers
     may cause a failure in badly designed PCI chips.

     There is currently no way to specify the caching mode for the mapping es‐
     tablished by the --DD option, ppcciiccoonnff always uses uncached access.  This is
     fine for control register BARs.

